WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:06.880
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am&nbsp;
going to explain the 2014 short comedy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:15.920
drama film called “Leonard in Slow Motion.”&nbsp;
Spoilers ahead! Watch out and take care!
&nbsp;

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:25.360
The protagonist of the movie is a middle-aged&nbsp;
man named Leonard who has a unique quality.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:32.480
He exists in slow motion but lives in a regular&nbsp;
speed world. Everything Leonard does is at a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:38.800
slower speed in general, not because he is lazy&nbsp;
but because it is just how he was born. His&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:45.600
drowsiness also applies to the things around him,&nbsp;
like the liquid he touches flows in slow motion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:49.760
defying all laws of physics. 
At the beginning of the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:54.720
we see him running to his workplace, in slow&nbsp;
motion of course, while the world around him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.720 --> 00:01:00.720
moves normally. At work, his colleagues make&nbsp;
fun of how he pours his coffee into a cup.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:06.320
They have worked with him for quite a while but&nbsp;
his unique quality never fails to surprise them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:12.000
Leonard has a crush on his colleague, Sheryl but&nbsp;
has never had the guts to confess to her. Every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:18.560
time he tries to talk to her, he stutters. Because&nbsp;
of that, plus his slowness, Leonard has never been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:25.120
able to utter a word to her. One day at work, his&nbsp;
boss calls him aside and praises him for coming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:31.680
to work early and leaving late, but complains&nbsp;
that his productivity is very low because of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:37.440
“quality”. To make up for it, he invites Leonard&nbsp;
to his kid’s birthday party as a performer. 
&nbsp;

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:43.840
Leonard reluctantly accepts the request and&nbsp;
performs tricks at his kid’s birthday. He bursts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:49.440
a water balloon in slow motion to entertain them.&nbsp;
It is clear from the trick that Leonard’s power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:55.920
bends the laws of physics. Sheryl, who is also at&nbsp;
the party, cheers for him. His boss knows that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:02.080
likes her and asks him to go start a conversation&nbsp;
with her. Leonard confidently approaches Sheryl&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:08.320
but stops when another guy starts talking to her&nbsp;
first. This has been a usual thing for Leonard.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:14.000
He is so slow that he is always preceded&nbsp;
by others in every aspect of his life.
&nbsp;

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:20.320
Later that day, he returns home in disappointment.&nbsp;
His day gets even worse when his boss calls to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:26.320
inform him that Sheryl is wanted at another one of&nbsp;
their offices, so she is moving to Florida within&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:31.760
a week. On the brighter side, his boss claims&nbsp;
that the kids were very happy at his arrival&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:36.720
and loved his water balloon trick. Leonard&nbsp;
knows that his boss is taking advantage of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:41.680
his uniqueness but he cannot quit his job&nbsp;
because he wouldn’t get one somewhere else.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:47.040
At night, While watching the TV, a news&nbsp;
report catches Leonard’s attention.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:53.200
An energy drink called the Shox beverage is&nbsp;
being sued for providing people with too much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:59.120
energy that they go into cardiac arrest. It turns&nbsp;
out that a malfunction caused a Chinese herbal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:05.840
stimulant called Chailow to overflow during the&nbsp;
production. Till now, a total of nine people have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:11.760
been hospitalized due to cardiac palpitations,&nbsp;
and dangerously hyperactive heart rate. 
&nbsp;

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:17.280
The advertisement of the drink says that one shot&nbsp;
of Shox will provide you with eight consecutive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:22.320
hours of energy. Although the news report&nbsp;
asks the people to not consume the beverage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:28.880
distributed within the last week, Leonard gets a&nbsp;
brilliant idea. He wants to try the energy drink&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:35.040
and see if it will increase his speed and turn&nbsp;
him like everyone else. However, he cannot find&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:40.720
the energy drink in shops as they have been told&nbsp;
to throw them away because of health reasons.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:46.240
So the next morning, Leonard brings his friend&nbsp;
to every dumpster in the town, looking for a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:52.800
pack of Shox that the shops have discarded. After&nbsp;
searching for hours, he finally finds a cartoon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:57.920
full of the drink in a garbage bin behind a&nbsp;
convenience store. In the following scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.920 --> 00:04:03.120
we see him chug down several bottles of the&nbsp;
energy drink, hoping it would make him normal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:10.000
Lo and beyond, the drink works and Leonard can&nbsp;
perform activities at a normal speed now.
&nbsp;

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:16.160
He speaks for the first time in the movie, and&nbsp;
says “this is amazing”. He then throws punches&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:22.000
in the air, fascinated by his own speed. Tying&nbsp;
his shoelace is an enjoyable task for him that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:27.200
morning. Even pouring himself a cup of coffee,&nbsp;
which doesn’t take forever to fill the cup,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:32.960
makes Leonard’s day. He puts more effort than&nbsp;
usual to run to work that day. Excited to do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:38.720
whatever he couldn’t when he was slow, Leonard&nbsp;
first tells his boss that he is quitting the job.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:44.320
He then runs to Sheryl who is in a meeting in&nbsp;
the boardroom. Leonard excitedly barges in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:50.160
disrupting the meeting, and says that he wants&nbsp;
to ask her a question. Sheryl and the rest of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:57.440
room anticipate the question but it never comes,&nbsp;
as at that moment, the effects of the energy drink&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:04.400
wear down. Sheryl asks him if he is okay to which&nbsp;
he embarrassingly and slowly replies that he is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:10.080
fine. All of a sudden, Leonard’s stomach starts&nbsp;
to grumble. The amount of energy drinks he had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:16.960
yesterday is finally making him sick. When no one&nbsp;
expects it, he projectile vomits through the room.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:24.000
His co-workers, including Sheryl, watch in disgust&nbsp;
as the vomit slowly falls all over the desk.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:29.360
Even his vomit doesn’t follow the rules of&nbsp;
gravity. Everyone then gets out of the room,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:34.960
leaving an embarrassed Leonard alone. His boss&nbsp;
comes in after a while and asks him to clean up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:40.960
the mess before leaving the job forever. 
In the following scene, Leonard walks into an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:47.360
old age home where he has gotten a new job to take&nbsp;
care of the old people. The job is perfect for him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:53.520
as the people there are as slow as him which&nbsp;
makes him feel included and normal. He is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:59.120
way happier there than he was at his previous&nbsp;
workplace. Leonard also writes a letter to Sheryl&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:04.880
apologizing for ruining her meeting and asking her&nbsp;
to visit the old age home as it is pretty close to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:10.720
the Florida office that she has transferred to.&nbsp;
In the last scene, Leonard is in a swimming pool&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:14.720
where Sheryl joins him, indicating that&nbsp;
they have finally started dating. 
&nbsp;

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:20.800
The fans have called “Leonard in slow motion”&nbsp;
a movie that is ahead of its time because of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:27.200
its bizarre, yet thoughtful concept and excellent&nbsp;
execution. Although it is only seven minutes long,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:32.880
it leaves an impression on every viewer. Some&nbsp;
fans have speculated several theories on what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:38.640
Leonard’s uniqueness denotes in real life. They&nbsp;
believe that it is meant to signify how people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:44.160
especially youngsters, feel like their life&nbsp;
is going slower than their friends and family.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:49.120
They are always comparing their achievements&nbsp;
to others, not realizing that they all have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:55.280
their own uniqueness as Leonard did. All of them&nbsp;
are going at their own pace and will eventually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.280 --> 00:07:00.800
achieve the things they want to. If they try&nbsp;
taking shortcuts to life, they might also end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.800 --> 00:07:16.160
up vomiting all over their workplace. 
